    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **48 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for `POST /api/owners`. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a different `telephone`, it is still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persisted fields `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) with getters/setters, mapped to new columns.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `findPossibleDuplicate(Owner)`, which runs after the hard-duplicate uniqueness check and finds the lowest-id non-deleted owner sharing the new owner's last name (case-insensitive) and postcode with a different telephone. Only owners that actually have a postcode participate. In `addOwner`, the result sets `possibleDuplicate` (true/false) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (matching id or null) before saving.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` as read-only fields on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct auto-maps them by name.\n\n4. **Schema (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`)** \u2014 Added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns. Tests run against hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema file is authoritative.\n\n5. **Seed data (`db/{hsqldb,mysql}/data.sql`)** \u2014 Those two DBs use positional `INSERT`s, so I appended two trailing `NULL`s per owner row to match the new column count (h2/postgres use named column lists and needed no change).\n\nThe new `Cp35Tests` passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
